    <h1>PixoraAI Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="date">
        Last Updated: October 1, 2026
    </p>

    <div class="card">

        <p>
            PixoraAI ("we", "our", "us", or "the app") is an AI-powered
            image editing and generation application.
        </p>

        <p>
            This Privacy Policy explains how PixoraAI handles information
            when you use our application.
        </p>

    </div>


    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

    <p>
        Depending on how you use PixoraAI, the application may process
        certain information.
    </p>

    <h3>Account Information</h3>

    <p>
        If you sign in with Google, PixoraAI may receive information such as
        your Google account name, email address, profile information, and a
        unique user identifier through Firebase Authentication.
    </p>

    <p>
        If you use Guest Login, PixoraAI creates an anonymous Firebase
        Authentication account with a unique identifier.
    </p>

    <h3>Images</h3>

    <p>
        When you select an image for AI generation, enhancement, or editing,
        the selected image is processed to provide the requested AI feature.
    </p>

    <p>
        The selected image may be transmitted to the third-party AI
        processing service used by PixoraAI.
    </p>

    <p>
        Generated images may be saved to your device when you choose to
        save them.
    </p>


    <h2>2. AI Image Processing</h2>

    <p>
        PixoraAI uses a third-party AI processing service hosted through
        Hugging Face to process images and generate AI results.
    </p>

    <p>
        When you use an AI image feature that requires an uploaded image,
        the selected image and the instructions required to process the
        image may be transmitted to that third-party AI service.
    </p>

    <p>
        Because the AI processing service is operated by a third party,
        its handling of information may also be subject to its own privacy
        policies and terms.
    </p>

    <p>
        PixoraAI does not claim that third-party AI services immediately
        delete submitted images unless such deletion is confirmed by the
        applicable service.
    </p>


    <h2>3. Advertising</h2>

    <p>
        PixoraAI uses Google Mobile Ads (AdMob), including rewarded
        advertisements.
    </p>

    <p>
        Advertising services may process information such as advertising
        identifiers and other device-related information to provide,
        measure, and improve advertising.
    </p>

    <p>
        Depending on the user's location, applicable laws, and consent
        choices, advertisements may be personalized, non-personalized,
        or limited.
    </p>

    <p>
        Rewarded advertisements may be shown when a user chooses to use
        certain PixoraAI features.
    </p>


    <h2>4. How We Use Information</h2>

    <p>Information processed by PixoraAI and its service providers may be used to:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Provide Google account authentication.</li>
        <li>Provide Guest account functionality.</li>
        <li>Provide AI image generation, enhancement, and editing.</li>
        <li>Process user-selected images for requested AI features.</li>
        <li>Display rewarded advertisements.</li>
        <li>Save generated images to the user's device when requested.</li>
        <li>Maintain application security.</li>
        <li>Prevent abuse and misuse of the application.</li>
        <li>Operate, maintain, and improve PixoraAI.</li>
    </ul>


    <h2>5. Sharing of Information</h2>

    <p>
        PixoraAI does not sell users' personal information.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information may be processed by third-party service providers
        that help us operate PixoraAI, including:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Google Firebase Authentication for account authentication.</li>
        <li>Google Mobile Ads (AdMob) for advertising.</li>
        <li>Hugging Face-hosted AI processing services for AI image processing.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        These third-party services may process information according to
        their own privacy policies, terms, and applicable laws.
    </p>


    <h2>6. Image Storage</h2>

    <p>
        Images selected for AI processing are temporarily handled by the
        application for processing.
    </p>

    <p>
        Generated images can be saved to the user's Android device in the
        PixoraAI image folder when the user chooses to save them.
    </p>

    <p>
        PixoraAI does not currently maintain a user-accessible cloud gallery
        containing users' generated images.
    </p>

    <p>
        Images saved directly to the user's device remain under the user's
        control.
    </p>


    <h2>7. Data Security</h2>

    <p>
        PixoraAI uses security mechanisms provided by the services used
        by the application.
    </p>

    <p>
        Firebase and other service providers may use encryption and other
        security measures to protect information.
    </p>

    <p>
        However, no method of electronic transmission or storage can be
        guaranteed to be completely secure.
    </p>


    <h2>8. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>

    <p>
        Firebase account information may be retained as necessary to provide
        account and authentication services.
    </p>

    <p>
        Users may request deletion of their PixoraAI account.
    </p>

    <p>
        When account deletion is requested and successfully processed,
        the associated PixoraAI/Firebase Authentication account will be
        deleted, subject to applicable legal requirements and information
        that third-party service providers may be required to retain.
    </p>

    <p>
        Images saved directly to the user's Android device are controlled
        by the user and are not automatically deleted when a PixoraAI
        account is deleted.
    </p>

    <p>
        Third-party services may have their own data retention and
        deletion policies.
    </p>


    <h2>9. Account Deletion</h2>

    <p>
        PixoraAI provides an account deletion process for users who create
        an account.
    </p>

    <p>
        Users can request deletion of their PixoraAI account from within
        the PixoraAI application and through the external account-deletion
        webpage provided by PixoraAI.
    </p>
<p>
    <a
        href="https://krishna0761.github.io/pixoraai-privacy/delete-account.html"
        target="_blank"
        style="color:#2F8CFF; font-weight:bold;">
        Request Account Deletion
    </a>
</p
    <p>
        Account deletion is different from logging out.
    </p>

    <p>
        Deleting an account is intended to remove the PixoraAI/Firebase
        Authentication account associated with the user, subject to
        applicable legal requirements and information that third-party
        service providers may be required to retain.
    </p>


    <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>

    <p>
        PixoraAI is not specifically directed toward children.
    </p>

    <p>
        We do not knowingly collect personal information from children
        in violation of applicable laws.
    </p>


    <h2>11. Third-Party Services</h2>

    <p>PixoraAI uses third-party services including:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Google Firebase Authentication</li>
        <li>Google Mobile Ads (AdMob)</li>
        <li>Hugging Face-hosted AI processing services</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        The privacy practices of these services are governed by their
        respective policies and terms.
    </p>


    <h2>12. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy when PixoraAI's features,
